WEBVTT

00:00:17.050 --> 00:00:18.660
Please forgive me...

00:00:19.870 --> 00:00:23.020
It's okay if you don't get any bigger.

00:00:23.020 --> 00:00:25.510
You'll always have me.

00:01:06.220 --> 00:01:08.080
Luda was crying.

00:01:09.580 --> 00:01:13.760
"I don't want to stay here. 
My heart will freeze."

00:01:14.470 --> 00:01:16.310
"Poor Luda."

00:01:16.310 --> 00:01:17.070
"Who's there?"

00:01:17.470 --> 00:01:20.420
"Have you forgotten about us?"

00:01:21.090 --> 00:01:26.750
When Luda looked up, she saw 
some familiar-looking fairies.

00:01:27.770 --> 00:01:29.370
"Come with us, Luda."

00:01:29.710 --> 00:01:34.440
"We have warm soup, blankets, 
and a pechka you can roll around in."

00:01:35.090 --> 00:01:37.400
"We can help you warm your frozen heart."

00:01:37.670 --> 00:01:39.990
Fairies are unscientific.

00:01:39.990 --> 00:01:41.770
Only children would believe that story.

00:01:44.710 --> 00:01:48.170
Natasha, there's more to 
this world than science.

00:01:49.980 --> 00:01:51.540
What else is there?

00:02:06.180 --> 00:02:07.680
<b>World Conquest
Zvezda Plot</b>

00:02:07.680 --> 00:02:10.390
<b>World Conquest
Zvezda Plot</b>

00:02:10.390 --> 00:02:13.020
<b>World Conquest
Zvezda Plot</b>

00:02:13.020 --> 00:02:14.690
<b>World Conquest
Zvezda Plot</b>

00:02:14.690 --> 00:02:15.440
<b>World Conquest
Zvezda Plot</b>

00:02:15.440 --> 00:02:15.770
<b>World Conquest
Zvezda Plot</b>

00:02:15.770 --> 00:02:16.060
<b>World Conquest
Zvezda Plot</b>

00:02:16.060 --> 00:02:16.730
<b>World Conquest
Zvezda Plot</b>

00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:28.770
This is good!

00:03:28.770 --> 00:03:30.520
Well done!

00:03:30.810 --> 00:03:33.220
Hey, cook! I want some more!

00:03:33.220 --> 00:03:34.280
Me, too!

00:03:34.570 --> 00:03:37.300
Yeah, yeah. It's coming!

00:03:38.140 --> 00:03:41.540
Kate! You have ketchup on your mouth!

00:03:41.540 --> 00:03:43.810
I'll get that off for you!

00:03:42.330 --> 00:03:43.810
Stop!

00:03:43.810 --> 00:03:46.260
What happened to your face, Dva?

00:03:46.820 --> 00:03:48.410
You have to ask?

00:03:50.420 --> 00:03:51.220
Hey.

00:03:54.260 --> 00:03:55.130
Yeah?

00:04:10.260 --> 00:04:13.450
He sneaked into Natasha's bed.

00:04:13.450 --> 00:04:14.600
He got what he deserved.

00:04:14.770 --> 00:04:16.670
You got it backwards! I'm innocent!

00:04:16.670 --> 00:04:18.090
Just let it slide.

00:04:18.090 --> 00:04:19.980
Natasha has a habit of sleepwalking.

00:04:20.650 --> 00:04:23.680
You should be overjoyed to have 
a teenage girl punch you!

00:04:27.660 --> 00:04:28.530
Huh?

00:04:28.720 --> 00:04:29.750
You're not gonna eat that?

00:04:29.750 --> 00:04:30.980
Oh, not exactly.

00:04:31.600 --> 00:04:36.040
I was thinking that raw udo has no 
taste, so I tried cooking it a bit.

00:04:36.040 --> 00:04:38.540
You bastard! What have you done?!

00:04:39.050 --> 00:04:41.270
Roboko can only eat raw udo!

00:04:41.640 --> 00:04:43.970
You've wasted her only source of energy!

00:04:44.400 --> 00:04:45.660
What?

00:04:45.660 --> 00:04:48.070
You could have said something sooner.

00:04:48.070 --> 00:04:50.680
But that was the last one...

00:04:50.990 --> 00:04:51.640
Okay!

00:04:52.380 --> 00:04:54.650
Here is your mission for the day, Dva.

00:04:54.650 --> 00:04:56.650
Secure a source of energy for Roboko!

00:04:56.860 --> 00:04:57.930
Source?

00:04:58.360 --> 00:04:59.850
Shouldn't you ask Natasha-san?

00:04:59.850 --> 00:05:02.900
It's your fault that Roboko is hungry, cook!

00:05:03.410 --> 00:05:04.870
I'm hungry.

00:05:05.850 --> 00:05:09.150
Roboko can no longer move an inch!

00:05:09.150 --> 00:05:11.860
Dva, carry out your mission!

00:05:12.240 --> 00:05:13.560
Yeah, yeah.

00:05:13.560 --> 00:05:15.880
So where do I go find some energy?

00:05:17.160 --> 00:05:18.670
The udo cellar in the basement.

00:05:19.170 --> 00:05:20.260
Udo cellar?

00:05:23.610 --> 00:05:24.210
<b>50 Meters Beneath</b>

00:05:24.210 --> 00:05:28.050
<b>50 Meters Beneath Zvezda Base</b>

00:05:28.500 --> 00:05:30.670
They grow udo down here?

00:05:31.230 --> 00:05:34.310
And it's not the udo I know.

00:05:36.350 --> 00:05:39.520
They just told me to pull 
two or three out, but...

00:05:43.450 --> 00:05:45.240
Whoa! W-Wait!

00:05:45.240 --> 00:05:46.730
<b>Meanwhile, inside the base kitchen</b>

00:05:54.720 --> 00:05:56.620
<i>Robo Butler!</i>

00:05:56.620 --> 00:05:58.330
Butler!

00:05:56.640 --> 00:05:58.320
<b>Simultaneously, in the command room</b>

00:05:59.490 --> 00:06:01.040
Wh-What?!

00:06:06.090 --> 00:06:07.880
The water!

00:06:10.870 --> 00:06:12.970
N-Natasha-san?!

00:06:15.880 --> 00:06:17.730
Hey, what's wrong?

00:06:17.730 --> 00:06:21.190
I never expected this to happen.

00:06:21.600 --> 00:06:23.470
We're in big trouble.

00:06:33.660 --> 00:06:33.910
<b>Zvezda</b>

00:06:33.910 --> 00:06:34.410
<b>Zvezda Emergency</b>

00:06:34.410 --> 00:06:35.490
<b>Zvezda Emergency Council</b>

00:06:35.720 --> 00:06:39.540
You're saying that without any 
power from the Udo Reactor,

00:06:39.540 --> 00:06:43.080
we can no longer transform?

00:06:43.370 --> 00:06:44.380
What?!

00:06:46.050 --> 00:06:47.370
That's right.

00:06:47.370 --> 00:06:51.250
And the stealth protection is weakened.

00:06:51.250 --> 00:06:52.390
Stealth protection?

00:06:52.650 --> 00:06:56.060
The only reason we can sleep soundly 
at night, while surrounded by the enemy,

00:06:56.300 --> 00:06:59.060
is because of the stealth 
device Natasha invented.

00:06:59.750 --> 00:07:03.320
The device is running on the 
emergency udo reserve right now,

00:07:03.320 --> 00:07:06.190
but the reserve will run out in 24 hours.

00:07:06.690 --> 00:07:07.940
Isn't that a big deal?!

00:07:08.220 --> 00:07:12.840
So I get that the udo field 
is important to Zvezda.

00:07:13.440 --> 00:07:17.410
But why did the udo suddenly die?

00:07:17.820 --> 00:07:20.180
Have you ever heard of a 
phenomenon where an entire

00:07:20.180 --> 00:07:22.080
bamboo forest will die off at once?

00:07:22.470 --> 00:07:26.090
The udo here dies every 
twelve thousand years.

00:07:26.310 --> 00:07:28.380
How would you know that?

00:07:28.790 --> 00:07:30.300
But it's too soon...

00:07:30.570 --> 00:07:32.010
Something is wrong...

00:07:33.740 --> 00:07:37.210
All udo is connected at the quantum level.

00:07:37.610 --> 00:07:41.190
Something must have happened 
to the parent udo root.

00:07:41.190 --> 00:07:42.190
That's it!

00:07:42.680 --> 00:07:45.860
We must find the parent root!

00:07:46.900 --> 00:07:48.330
Parent root, huh?

00:07:48.330 --> 00:07:51.080
Do you expect all of us to
dig up the entire field?

00:07:51.960 --> 00:07:52.740
All of us?

00:07:52.740 --> 00:07:53.630
Huh?

00:07:54.210 --> 00:07:55.280
Come to think of it...

00:07:56.370 --> 00:07:59.170
We seem to be forgetting something...

00:08:00.490 --> 00:08:01.470
It's not important.

00:08:01.470 --> 00:08:02.370
Natasha!

00:08:02.370 --> 00:08:04.500
Yep, this is the udo root radar.

00:08:04.520 --> 00:08:08.450
<b>Quantum Interference Scanner</b>

00:08:05.020 --> 00:08:07.780
We can use it to track down the parent root.

00:08:10.280 --> 00:08:13.960
It's underneath Udogawa, 
but it's down deep.

00:08:13.960 --> 00:08:15.050
As I thought.

00:08:15.050 --> 00:08:17.440
Udo that can live twelve thousand years...

00:08:17.440 --> 00:08:18.920
underneath Udogawa?

00:08:21.080 --> 00:08:23.020
What's waiting down there?

00:08:24.000 --> 00:08:25.180
There is

00:08:27.910 --> 00:08:30.190
the ancient Udogawa civilization!

00:08:30.440 --> 00:08:32.950
Wh-What did you say?!

00:08:33.700 --> 00:08:36.960
<b>World Conquest
Zvezda Plot</b>

00:08:34.300 --> 00:08:36.940
<b>Episode 4                       Udo's in the Cold Ground</b>

00:08:37.700 --> 00:08:40.960
<b>World Conquest
Zvezda Plot</b>

00:08:38.300 --> 00:08:40.940
<b>Episode 4                       Udo's in the Cold Ground</b>

00:08:41.950 --> 00:08:46.910
<b>500 Meters Beneath West Udogawa City</b>

00:08:47.310 --> 00:08:49.870
<b>Ancient Udogawa Ruins: 13th Floor</b>

00:08:50.740 --> 00:08:52.220
I had no idea that the

00:08:52.220 --> 00:08:54.510
ruins of an ancient civilization 
rested under West Udogawa.

00:08:55.150 --> 00:08:58.790
They must have been fans 
of dark and creepy places.

00:08:58.790 --> 00:09:02.100
Humans can't survive without some sunlight.

00:09:02.100 --> 00:09:04.060
<b>Shortcut</b>

00:09:02.100 --> 00:09:04.060
<b>1 time 500 yen</b>

00:09:02.450 --> 00:09:04.060
Even Natasha-san thinks they 
didn't get out enough!

00:09:04.450 --> 00:09:07.100
I have a feeling that 
Goro-san and Itsuka-san

00:09:07.100 --> 00:09:09.820
would be better for work that 
requires brute strength.

00:09:10.260 --> 00:09:14.930
We need them to guard the base 
in case something happens.

00:09:14.930 --> 00:09:16.470
That's right.

00:09:16.830 --> 00:09:20.020
Every person has a role to play...

00:09:22.340 --> 00:09:24.820
It's almost time for an afternoon nap.

00:09:24.820 --> 00:09:26.080
You're such a child.

00:09:27.650 --> 00:09:30.500
You're the one who sleepwalks, Natasha-san.

00:09:31.030 --> 00:09:35.510
Your room was rather 
comfortable for sleeping.

00:09:40.160 --> 00:09:42.620
Shouldn't we act normal?

00:09:42.620 --> 00:09:44.250
We've been told to guard the 
house while they're gone,

00:09:44.250 --> 00:09:46.760
so we need to stay sharp.

00:09:47.200 --> 00:09:48.270
I see.

00:09:49.990 --> 00:09:51.080
Wait!

00:09:51.080 --> 00:09:53.280
Hey, Pops! Where do you think you're going?

00:09:54.070 --> 00:09:55.740
To procure provisions.

00:09:55.740 --> 00:09:59.170
You probably just want to buy 
your fancy little sweets.

00:09:59.610 --> 00:10:01.310
Send Roboko, then.

00:10:01.840 --> 00:10:03.200
Actually...

00:10:03.830 --> 00:10:05.910
Roboko isn't around.

00:10:06.940 --> 00:10:08.120
She's missing?

00:10:09.400 --> 00:10:12.030
<b>Ancient Udogawa Ruins: 24th Floor</b>

00:10:16.870 --> 00:10:20.760
Is this girl really serious 
about conquering the world?

00:10:27.650 --> 00:10:28.660
What?

00:10:28.660 --> 00:10:30.030
Oh, uh...

00:10:30.570 --> 00:10:33.300
I was just thinking that 
you looked really calm.

00:10:33.740 --> 00:10:35.770
Considering how we're in 
such a strange place...

00:10:36.860 --> 00:10:39.140
I've been here before.

00:10:40.690 --> 00:10:41.660
When was that?

00:10:41.870 --> 00:10:43.360
It was

00:10:44.540 --> 00:10:46.660
back when I was still in the Ukraine.

00:10:47.140 --> 00:10:48.720
Wait, where?

00:10:48.720 --> 00:10:49.820
Ukraine?

00:10:49.820 --> 00:10:51.290
How old are you?

00:10:51.570 --> 00:10:55.340
You fool! I'm a lovely fifteen-year-old!

00:10:55.340 --> 00:10:56.530
Fifteen?

00:10:56.530 --> 00:10:59.540
Oh, so you're only one year older than me.

00:10:59.540 --> 00:11:01.300
Show some more respect!

00:11:01.510 --> 00:11:03.210
You're just a lowly soldier.

00:11:03.210 --> 00:11:05.640
I'm Professor Um, one of the leaders!

00:11:08.830 --> 00:11:10.560
Wh-What was that?

00:11:10.910 --> 00:11:13.630
There was something there... right?

00:11:14.430 --> 00:11:16.050
It might be the fairies.

00:11:16.420 --> 00:11:18.140
Fairies?

00:11:18.620 --> 00:11:21.400
Like the small pixies that fly around?

00:11:21.400 --> 00:11:22.280
That's right.

00:11:22.740 --> 00:11:25.660
No way. This isn't some fairy tale.

00:11:31.030 --> 00:11:32.800
H-Hey...

00:11:34.820 --> 00:11:36.620
You already know that

00:11:36.620 --> 00:11:39.490
I was a big fan of mechas 
from a young age, right?

00:11:39.490 --> 00:11:41.840
I didn't know that until you told me now.

00:11:42.630 --> 00:11:45.580
My parents were scientists,

00:11:45.580 --> 00:11:48.210
so there were plenty of 
tools and books around.

00:11:48.760 --> 00:11:51.430
Even though I was a kid,

00:11:51.430 --> 00:11:55.310
I would build dangerous things 
and scare the neighbor kids.

00:11:56.920 --> 00:11:58.910
After a while,

00:11:58.910 --> 00:12:02.300
nobody would play with me 
anymore because I creeped them out.

00:12:02.990 --> 00:12:06.540
But I was still happy.

00:12:08.810 --> 00:12:13.960
But the neighbors probably pitied 
me and thought I was strange.

00:12:14.890 --> 00:12:18.630
A kid obsessed with things 
that weren't of this world.

00:12:19.420 --> 00:12:20.880
And can I really blame them?

00:12:32.190 --> 00:12:33.700
Stop it, Natasha.

00:12:34.490 --> 00:12:35.400
Papa...

00:12:35.770 --> 00:12:38.470
You're all by yourself again, poor thing.

00:12:38.470 --> 00:12:39.530
Mama...

00:13:04.700 --> 00:13:05.630
Where are we going?

00:13:08.300 --> 00:13:10.100
We're going to the kingdom of fairies.

00:13:11.410 --> 00:13:12.640
Fairies?

00:13:13.170 --> 00:13:14.020
That's right.

00:13:14.680 --> 00:13:17.650
It's a kingdom where you can be happy.

00:13:48.990 --> 00:13:52.310
I don't remember what happened next.

00:13:53.570 --> 00:14:00.540
I spent days, perhaps years 
wandering through the darkness.

00:14:14.200 --> 00:14:16.010
With Roboko by my side.

00:14:18.380 --> 00:14:22.540
It's possible that I could 
see fairies in the darkness.

00:14:23.270 --> 00:14:26.130
And what about your parents?

00:14:26.600 --> 00:14:27.900
They're missing.

00:14:28.760 --> 00:14:31.830
That was when we met Kate.

00:14:33.710 --> 00:14:36.190
When we returned to the surface,

00:14:36.190 --> 00:14:39.310
we were in West Udogawa for some reason.

00:14:39.310 --> 00:14:42.390
What? You went from 
Ukraine to West Udogawa?

00:14:42.390 --> 00:14:43.390
How?

00:14:44.490 --> 00:14:46.440
And what was the ancient 
Udogawa civilization?

00:14:46.930 --> 00:14:48.550
What happened to the fairies?

00:14:50.650 --> 00:14:53.340
I traveled a little too far if 
I wanted to run away from home.

00:14:54.990 --> 00:14:58.790
I still have no idea what 
happened back then.

00:14:59.490 --> 00:15:02.730
I just knew that Kate had saved my life.

00:15:03.770 --> 00:15:06.760
So I swore fealty to Kate.

00:15:07.820 --> 00:15:10.720
Come to think of it, 
you also ran away from home.

00:15:12.950 --> 00:15:18.640
I can't remember when my parents let 
go of my hands in the darkness.

00:15:19.130 --> 00:15:22.690
It's possible that I was the one who let go.

00:15:24.760 --> 00:15:26.390
Maybe it was for the better.

00:15:30.950 --> 00:15:31.960
It disappeared?

00:15:32.370 --> 00:15:34.240
The signal from the parent root disappeared!

00:15:34.500 --> 00:15:37.870
What?! Are we lost in the 
middle of nowhere now?!

00:15:39.350 --> 00:15:40.750
We're lost?

00:15:40.750 --> 00:15:42.370
You finally woke up?

00:15:44.380 --> 00:15:46.000
The signal disappeared?

00:15:46.000 --> 00:15:51.870
That means the parent root 
is dead or very weak!

00:15:51.870 --> 00:15:52.510
We must hurry!

00:16:01.420 --> 00:16:03.180
I-It's

00:16:04.140 --> 00:16:05.700
a tree of udo!

00:16:11.510 --> 00:16:12.800
It's dying?

00:16:21.340 --> 00:16:22.210
What?

00:16:23.840 --> 00:16:25.670
Wh-What is that thing?!

00:16:25.950 --> 00:16:29.730
A fairy? More like some kind of earthworm...

00:16:29.730 --> 00:16:30.550
It's the enemy!

00:16:31.170 --> 00:16:34.870
A parasite that represents the 
manifestation of human fear!

00:16:34.870 --> 00:16:36.430
You just made that up, didn't you?

00:16:40.640 --> 00:16:45.090
Say, what do they look like to you?

00:16:45.090 --> 00:16:46.870
What do they look like to me?

00:16:48.130 --> 00:16:53.570
Like a hazy cloud that represents 
the manifestation of human fear?

00:16:56.170 --> 00:16:57.870
I see how it is.

00:16:58.620 --> 00:17:01.560
If they get close to the udo, it's over!

00:17:01.560 --> 00:17:03.380
I'll handle them!

00:17:03.380 --> 00:17:04.600
You take it from here!

00:17:04.600 --> 00:17:06.620
Wait, what am I supposed to do?!

00:17:06.620 --> 00:17:07.250
Up there!

00:17:08.490 --> 00:17:11.260
You make the stamen and pistil ****!

00:17:11.260 --> 00:17:13.300
Don't make it sound dirty!

00:17:13.300 --> 00:17:15.360
So you want me to help pollinate the plant?

00:17:15.360 --> 00:17:17.960
No, this is a sacred ceremony 
that rivals the rituals from

00:17:17.960 --> 00:17:19.680
the stories about the genesis of this world!

00:17:20.090 --> 00:17:22.520
Enough chatter! Just go!

00:17:32.690 --> 00:17:35.200
'Kay now, take this!

00:17:48.570 --> 00:17:50.210
Natasha...

00:17:50.950 --> 00:17:53.300
Over here, Natasha...

00:17:58.690 --> 00:18:00.190
Natasha...

00:18:00.790 --> 00:18:02.850
Natasha...

00:18:02.850 --> 00:18:03.930
Natasha...

00:18:03.930 --> 00:18:05.310
Natasha...

00:18:05.310 --> 00:18:06.470
Natasha...

00:18:06.470 --> 00:18:08.060
Natasha...

00:18:09.590 --> 00:18:10.660
Natasha-san!

00:18:11.780 --> 00:18:12.760
Natasha...

00:18:12.760 --> 00:18:14.490
Natasha...

00:18:14.490 --> 00:18:15.770
Natasha...

00:18:15.770 --> 00:18:17.070
Natasha...

00:18:19.410 --> 00:18:20.790
I apologize for arriving late.

00:18:20.790 --> 00:18:21.660
Roboko!

00:18:23.070 --> 00:18:24.620
Get 'em, Roboko!

00:18:37.860 --> 00:18:39.280
Wh-What do we do?!

00:18:39.280 --> 00:18:40.140
I don't know!

00:18:40.600 --> 00:18:42.510
You don't know?!

00:18:44.150 --> 00:18:45.060
We do this!

00:18:48.550 --> 00:18:49.990
L-Like this?!

00:18:57.200 --> 00:18:58.630
Hang in there, Roboko!

00:18:58.630 --> 00:19:00.950
Expel those ghosts from the past!

00:19:13.450 --> 00:19:14.400
This is...

00:20:04.460 --> 00:20:07.720
Okay, we should be safe 
for another week now.

00:20:07.720 --> 00:20:08.940
That's it?!

00:20:08.940 --> 00:20:10.770
We went from twelve thousand 
years to seven days?

00:20:11.160 --> 00:20:14.520
Oh, Roboko. How were you able to move?

00:20:14.520 --> 00:20:17.230
Yeah, I thought you were out of energy.

00:20:22.220 --> 00:20:26.330
Roboko, you can eat cooked udo now?!

00:20:30.950 --> 00:20:33.260
You've gotten over your 
dislike of cooked udo.

00:20:33.260 --> 00:20:34.670
Wait, what?

00:20:34.670 --> 00:20:37.170
Sh-She's just a picky eater?!

00:20:38.220 --> 00:20:41.630
Asuta-san worked hard to cook it for me.

00:20:43.410 --> 00:20:44.090
Huh?

00:20:47.010 --> 00:20:48.490
I'm gonna die!

00:20:58.380 --> 00:21:00.650
You have nowhere to go?

00:21:00.970 --> 00:21:03.360
But you can do whatever you want.

00:21:03.360 --> 00:21:05.110
Yes, is that a problem?

00:21:05.110 --> 00:21:08.020
In that case, will you join me in conquest?

00:21:09.220 --> 00:21:12.100
I only know how to do one thing,

00:21:12.100 --> 00:21:14.670
but I'll be traveling the 
whole world in the process.

00:21:18.830 --> 00:21:21.920
Then I'll help you conquer the world.

00:21:38.940 --> 00:21:39.650
Let's go.

00:21:39.250 --> 00:21:40.070
Huh? Wha?!

00:21:40.070 --> 00:21:42.940
S-Sunlight! We made it back!

00:21:48.890 --> 00:21:50.310
There's...

00:21:50.820 --> 00:21:52.390
Enough to start our own business.

00:21:52.950 --> 00:21:55.070
Why don't we try that?

00:21:55.070 --> 00:21:55.790
Huh?

00:21:56.140 --> 00:21:59.670
Where did you go during our time of crisis?!

00:21:59.670 --> 00:22:01.030
I'm sorry.

00:22:01.030 --> 00:22:03.130
Stuff kept coming up, you see...

00:22:03.430 --> 00:22:05.030
So what?

00:22:05.030 --> 00:22:07.300
We almost died when our stuff came up!

00:22:07.640 --> 00:22:09.440
Well, what can I say...

00:23:46.900 --> 00:23:50.530
West Udogawa Market

00:23:50.530 --> 00:23:52.160
<b>We Have Super Ancient 
Udogawa Ice Cream.
1 For 150 yen</b>

00:23:50.840 --> 00:23:52.160
<b>Super Ancient Udogawa Ice Cream</b>

00:23:52.550 --> 00:23:55.570
<b>Super Ancient Udogawa Sweet Buns</b>

00:23:53.800 --> 00:23:55.580
<b>Super Ancient Udogawa Soba</b>

00:23:55.930 --> 00:23:59.910
<b>Super Ancient Udogawa Civilization</b>

00:23:57.710 --> 00:23:59.910
<b>Conquered</b>

00:23:59.910 --> 00:24:02.380
<b>World Conquest
Zvezda Plot</b>

00:24:00.820 --> 00:24:04.960
My name is Odin. I'm known 
to bring women to tears.

00:24:04.960 --> 00:24:08.540
I see, the kid's gotten to that age.

00:24:08.540 --> 00:24:10.430
How bittersweet.

00:24:10.430 --> 00:24:13.760
Now fight, kid! You're up against the world!

00:24:13.760 --> 00:24:16.070
You can only trust yourself!

00:24:16.070 --> 00:24:18.410
When nobody else supports you,

00:24:18.410 --> 00:24:20.290
you know you're doing something worthwhile.

00:24:20.290 --> 00:24:22.020
What is this letter?

00:24:22.020 --> 00:24:23.850
To my beloved Lady Plamya?

00:24:24.490 --> 00:24:26.500
I was a young fool.

00:24:26.500 --> 00:24:29.030
I didn't want to hear that!

00:24:26.960 --> 00:24:30.420
<b>Episode 5                     White Robin in Danger!</b>
